-- title:
--   Chart values of compatible sections are Γ'-invariant
-- statement:
--   The statement is formulated inside the full Čerednik–Drinfeld set-up for the formal uniformisation; the hypotheses are grouped below, and the conclusion is stated in full at the end.
--
--   **Arithmetic base.** A prime $r$; a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), subject to `hcomplete` ($\mathcal O$ is adically complete for the ideal $(\pi)$), `hres` (the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements) and `hunr` (the ideals $(r)$ and $(\pi)$ of $\mathcal O$ coincide, so $\mathcal O$ is absolutely unramified); and a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified layer.** A characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$ of $Onr$, subject to: `hOnr_complete` ($Onr$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$), `hOnr_max` (that ideal is maximal), `hOnr_alg` (every element of $Onr$ satisfies, modulo $\pi$, a monic polynomial with coefficients in $\mathcal O$), `hOnr_closed` (every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$), and `hFr` ($Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ for all $x$), so that $Fr$ is a Frobenius lift on a complete unramified extension with algebraically closed residue field. Write $Onr_2$ for the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of elements fixed by $Fr^{2}$ (the equaliser of $Fr\circ Fr$ and the identity).
--
--   **Determinant valuation.** A group homomorphism $vdet$ from $GL_2(K_0)$ to $\mathbb Z$ written multiplicatively, characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g)$ equals $n$ exactly when $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$. Below $v(g)$ denotes the integer underlying $vdet(g)$.
--
--   **Group data.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma : G\to GL_2(K_0)$, a subgroup $\Gamma\le G$, with `hcent` (there is $z\in\Gamma$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix $c\cdot 1$ and $v(\sigma z)=2$) and `hodd` (there is $w\in\Gamma$ with $v(\sigma w)=1$); a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by `hΓ'` as the set of elements of $\Gamma$ with $v(\sigma x)$ even; a homomorphism $\rho : G\to PGL_2(K_0)$ with `hρ` ($\rho g$ is the class of $\sigma g$); `hdisc` (for each vertex of the lattice tree of $\mathcal O$ in $K_0$, its stabiliser in $\rho(\Gamma')$ is finite) and `hcocpt` (a finite set of vertices meeting every $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit); the matrix $g_1$ with `hg₁`: $g_1 = \mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$; a subgroup $N$ of $PGL_2(K_0)$ with `hNle` ($N\le\rho(\Gamma')$), `hNnorm` (the preimage of $N$ in $\rho(\Gamma)$ is normal there) and `hNidx` (the relative index of $N$ in $\rho(\Gamma')$ is non-zero).
--
--   **The Mumford tower `DM`.** A term of `MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`: schemes $Z_n$ with structure maps $zb_n : Z_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $zt_n : Z_n\to Z_{n+1}$ exhibiting each $Z_n$ as the base change of $Z_{n+1}$ along $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+2}\to\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, with $zb_n$ proper and flat, every finite subset of $Z_n$ contained in an affine open, and a modular map $q$ assigning to each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$ in $B$ and each Deligne datum $P$ over $B$ a $B$-point of $Z_n$, compatible with the base, natural in $B$, compatible with the transitions, and invariant under translating $P$ by an element of $GL_2(K_0)$ whose class lies in $N$; the remaining fields, which provide open-immersion charts from the edge chart rings, are summarised here. Here a *Deligne datum* over $B$ (the objects of the functor `Omega K₀ π`) assigns to every full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M\subset K_0^2$ a $B$-submodule $\mathrm{line}(M)\subseteq B\otimes_{\mathcal O}M$ with invertible quotient, monotone in $M$, equivariant for homotheties, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$; and `DeligneDatum.IsPullback B g d d'` says that $d'.\mathrm{line}(M)$ is the preimage of $d.\mathrm{line}(g\cdot M)$ under the base-changed action isomorphism, for every $M$.
--
--   **The auxiliary tower and its data.** Schemes $X_n$ with $xb_n : X_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $xt_n$; a finite group $G_2$ acting by $a_n : G_2\to\mathrm{Aut}(X_n)$; projections $pr_1{}_n : X_n\to Z_n$ and $pr_2{}_n : X_n\to\operatorname{Spec}(Onr_2/\pi^{n+1})$; a homomorphism $\theta : \Gamma\to G_2$; and $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphisms $Fr_2{}_n$ of $Onr_2/\pi^{n+1}$. The hypotheses are: `hcart` (the tower $X$ is cartesian over the base quotients), `hproper` and `hflat` ($xb_n$ proper, flat), `haff` (finite subsets of $X_n$ lie in affine opens), `ha_over` and `ha_xt` (the $G_2$-action is over the base and commutes with the transitions), `hX` (each $X_n$ is the fibre product of $Z_n$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(Onr_2/\pi^{n+1})$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$, via $pr_1$ and $pr_2$), `hxb`, `hxt₁`, `hxt₂` (the projections are compatible with the structure maps and the transitions on both factors), `hθsurj` ($\theta$ is surjective), `hθker` ($\theta\gamma=1$ iff $\rho\gamma\in N$), `hFr₂` ($Fr_2{}_n$ is induced by $Fr$ on the fixed ring), `ha_pr₂` (for $\gamma\in\Gamma$ the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ followed by $pr_2{}_n$ equals $pr_2{}_n$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $Fr_2{}_n^{-v(\sigma\gamma)}$) and `ha_pr₁` (if $P'$ is the $\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}$-pullback of $P$ over a $\pi^{n+1}$-torsion $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ and a $B$-point $x$ of $X_n$ satisfies $pr_1{}_n\circ x = DM.q_n(P)$, then $pr_1{}_n\circ a_n(\theta\gamma)\circ x = DM.q_n(P')$).
--
--   **The quotient tower `DQ` and its modular map.** A term `DQ` of `TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`: schemes $Y_n$ over $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ with cartesian transitions, proper and flat structure maps, and maps $p_n : X_n\to Y_n$ over the base, compatible with and cartesian over the transitions, invariant under the $G_2$-action, finite, surjective, locally epimorphic over every open, and satisfying a local universal property; the further fields are summarised here. Next, a map $q$ sending, for each $n$ and each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi^{n+1}=0$, a pair consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $Onr\to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ (the objects of `AlgFunctor.prod (AlgFunctor.corep Onr) (Omega K₀ π)`) to a $B$-point of $Y_n$, subject to: `hqdef` (if $\psi : Onr\to B$, if $\psi_2 : Onr_2/\pi^{n+1}\to B$ is induced by $\psi$, and if a $B$-point $x$ of $X_n$ satisfies $pr_1{}_n\circ x = DM.q_n(P)$ and $pr_2{}_n\circ x = \operatorname{Spec}(\psi_2)$, then $q_n(\psi,P) = p_n\circ x$), `hqover` (compatibility with the structure map to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$), `hqnat` (naturality in $B$), `hqyt` (compatibility with the transitions $yt_n$) and `hqinv` (for $\gamma\in\Gamma$, $q_n$ takes the same value on $x$ and on any $x'$ with `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B (σ γ) x x'`, that is, $x'_1 = x_1\circ Fr^{-v(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $x'_2$ is the $\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}$-pullback of $x_2$).
--
--   **The unramified presentation and its quotient.** A term `Pr` of `MumfordTower.NrPresentation` for the above data and the subgroup $\theta(\Gamma')\le G_2$ (the image under $\theta$ of $\Gamma'$ regarded inside $\Gamma$): schemes $X'_n$ over $Onr/\pi^{n+1}$ with transitions and a $G_2$-action, maps $qX_n : X'_n\to X_n$ exhibiting $X'_n$ as the base change of $X_n$ along $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}\to Onr/\pi^{n+1}$, the corresponding compatibilities, and charts $\kappa'_{h,n}$ from $\operatorname{Spec}A_n$ to $X'_n$ for each $h\in GL_2(K_0)$, where $A_n$ denotes $\mathrm{chartERing}(Onr,\pi,r)$ — the localisation of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2,Onr)$ modulo the edge relation away from the discriminant element — reduced modulo the $(n+1)$-st power of the image of $\pi$; the modular characterisation of the charts and the remaining fields are summarised here. Further: a term `D'` of `TowerQuotientDatum` for the tower $X'$ with its $G_2$-action, with schemes $Y'_n$ and quotient maps $p'_n : X'_n\to Y'_n$; maps $rY_n : Y'_n\to Y_n$ with `hrY` (each $Y'_n$ is the base change of $Y_n$ along $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}\to Onr/\pi^{n+1}$), `hrY_p` ($p'_n$ followed by $rY_n$ equals $qX_n$ followed by $p_n$) and `hrY_yt` (compatibility with the transitions).
--
--   **Chart opens and chart coordinates.** For each $h\in GL_2(K_0)$ and $n$ an open $U_{h,n}$ of $Y'_n$ with `hU`: its underlying set is the image of the base map of $\kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $p'_n$; a ring homomorphism $c_{h,n}$ from the sections of $Y'_n$ over $U_{h,n}$ to $A_n$; `hκU` (the preimage of $U_{h,n}$ under $\kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $p'_n$ is the whole of $\operatorname{Spec}A_n$) and `hc` ($c_{h,n}(s)$ is the pullback of $s$ along $\kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $p'_n$, read as an element of $A_n$ through the canonical isomorphism between $A_n$ and the global sections of $\operatorname{Spec}A_n$).
--
--   **The family of sections.** A fixed $h\in GL_2(K_0)$; a family $\mathrm{fam}(m)\in A_m$ with `hfam` (the transition map $A_{m+1}\to A_m$ carries $\mathrm{fam}(m+1)$ to $\mathrm{fam}(m)$); a family of sections $s_m$ of $Y'_m$ over $U_{h,m}$ with `hs` (the pullback of $s_{m+1}$ along $yt'_m$, restricted to $U_{h,m}$, equals $s_m$); and `hsc` ($c_{h,m}(s_m)=\mathrm{fam}(m)$ for every $m$).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $m$, every commutative ring $B$ carrying compatible $\mathcal O$- and $Onr$-algebra structures in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, every pair of $Onr$-algebra homomorphisms $\bar x,\bar x' : A_m\to B$, and all Deligne data $d,d',P,P'$ over $B$ (relative to $\pi$ and $K_0$), the following implication holds. Assume first that $d$ lies in the edge chart with coordinates given by $\bar x$: the submodule $d.\mathrm{line}$ at the standard full lattice is the $B$-span of $\bar x(\xi)\otimes_{\mathcal O}e_0 + 1\otimes_{\mathcal O}e_1$, the submodule $d.\mathrm{line}$ at $g_1\cdot(\text{standard lattice})$ is the image, under the base-changed action isomorphism `actBaseChange B g₁`, of the $B$-span of $1\otimes_{\mathcal O}e_0+\bar x(\eta)\otimes_{\mathcal O}e_1$, and `d.InEdgeChart π (g₁ · std) std` holds, i.e. at every prime $\mathfrak p$ of $B$ the pair $(g_1\cdot\mathrm{std},\mathrm{std})$ is an edge along which $d$ is non-degenerate in the sense of `DeligneDatum.EdgeNondegAt`; here $\xi$ and $\eta$ are the two distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η` of the edge chart ring, taken modulo $\pi^{m+1}$, and $e_0,e_1$ are the standard basis vectors of the standard lattice. Assume the same three conditions for $d'$ with $\bar x'$ in place of $\bar x$. Assume further that $P$ is the $h^{-1}$-pullback of $d$ and $P'$ the $h^{-1}$-pullback of $d'$, both in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback`, and that there exists $\gamma\in\Gamma'$ such that $P'$ is the $\sigma(\gamma)^{-1}$-pullback of $P$. Then
--   $$\bar x(\mathrm{fam}(m)) = \bar x'(\mathrm{fam}(m))$$
--   in $B$; that is, the chart value $c_{h,m}(s_m)$ of the section $s_m$ takes the same value at the two chart points $\bar x$ and $\bar x'$.
--
--   This is the invariance half of the "functions" clause in the construction of the unramified layer of the Čerednik–Drinfeld formal uniformisation: a compatible family of sections of the quotient tower $Y'$ over a chart open has a chart value whose evaluation at a chart point depends only on the $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit of the associated Deligne datum. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions), and the proof cites [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.OmegaNr.isTwistedAct_laws`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.OmegaNr.isTwistedAct_laws) for the formal properties of the Frobenius-twisted action on pairs consisting of a homomorphism out of $Onr$ and a Deligne datum.
